// The seeded encoder-differential corpus, as the gate every build runs.
// The twelve variants and their expected sealed identities are checked
// in (Inputs/fuzz-corpus.{mlir,ids}); the generator that minted them is
// the reference twin's fuzz module, and fuzz-roundtrip.test — gated on
// uv — is what keeps the checked-in corpus equal to what the generator
// produces today. Splitting it this way is deliberate: the primary
// encoding gate must run where uv is absent, so the corpus is checked
// in and the generator becomes what refreshes it.
//
// The gates over the corpus:
//   1. every variant seals (valid-by-construction is real, not assumed);
//   2. the sealed artifact is parse -> print -> parse stable;
//   3. the sealed identities equal the pinned ones, in order — encode
//      determinism against values minted on the other leg.
// RUN: zkc-opt %pir-seal-full %S/Inputs/fuzz-corpus.mlir -o %t.sealed
// RUN: zkc-opt %t.sealed -o %t.reprint
// RUN: diff %t.sealed %t.reprint
// RUN: grep -o 'id "[0-9a-f]*"' %t.sealed > %t.got.ids
// RUN: diff %t.got.ids %S/Inputs/fuzz-corpus.ids
